course: dictionary
lesson: 15167
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words can do more than one job in a sentence. The job a word does is its part of speech: a noun names a thing, and a verb shows an action. The word scrapbook can do both jobs. «I put my bus ticket in my scrapbook.» Here scrapbook is a noun, the thing you keep.
explain: «Every summer we scrapbook our holidays.» Now scrapbook is a verb, an action that means making scrapbooks as a hobby. Ask yourself: is this word a thing, or is it something people do? The words around it are the clues, which is context again.
explain: Check the clues. In «We found an old scrapbook in the attic», the words "an old" and "in the attic" show a thing. In «We scrapbooked all afternoon», the words "all afternoon" show an action that goes on for a while.
fact: A scrapbook is a book with blank pages where you stick pictures, tickets, photos, cuttings and notes.
fact: People keep scrapbooks to remember things, such as trips, birthdays or school projects.
fact: As a verb, to scrapbook means to make scrapbooks as a hobby. It is informal, so it is best used in chatty writing, not formal essays.
fact: In a school project, a scrapbook can collect pictures and facts on one topic.
fact: The plural of the noun is scrapbooks. The past tense of the verb is scrapbooked.
exercise: «Mum keeps all our holiday tickets in a scrapbook.» What job does scrapbook do here? | An adjective, describing a word | A verb, an action | *A noun, a thing you keep | An adverb, telling how
exercise: «Every Sunday we scrapbook together and laugh at the old photos.» What does scrapbook mean here? | To read a book quietly | To pack a bag for a trip | To tear up old pictures | *To make scrapbooks as a hobby
exercise: Which is the plural of scrapbook? | scrapbookses | scrapbooky | *scrapbooks
test: «In the attic we found Grandma's scrapbook, full of old photos.» What is a scrapbook? | A box for storing shoes | A type of school bag | A map of the town | *A book with blank pages for sticking in pictures, tickets and notes
test: Which sentence uses scrapbook as a verb? | «I bought a new scrapbook today.» | «She filled three scrapbooks last year.» | «The scrapbook had a red cover.» | *«We scrapbooked our trip to the seaside.»
exam: Why might a child make a scrapbook for a school project? | To learn to swim | *To collect pictures and facts on one topic | To sell old furniture | To make a room darker
